Skiff v2.1.1 – studio twin (firmware code for the host), built from https://github.com/illuminus5/skiff tag v2.1.1
(commit 48e77fda5916e9a5ba9e7339161f719d8877ce49; source: https://github.com/illuminus5/skiff/archive/48e77fda5916e9a5ba9e7339161f719d8877ce49.tar.gz).
GPL-3.0-only. Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita (@kurogedelic), Hügelton Instruments (Felucca); Copyright (C) 2026 illuminus5 (Skiff's changes and additions).
Ported parts keep their licences (DaisySP and Rings: MIT, msfa: Apache-2.0; the UI font Barlow Condensed and the Fukiai icons are rasterised in: OFL 1.1, MIT), the instrument samples are CC0 (Versilian Studios):
Skiff's LICENSING.md and the texts in THIRD_PARTY.txt beside this file.
The firmware sources are unmodified. The glue tools/studio/skiff_studio.c (GPL-3.0-only, in FM-1 Companion's source) includes them as Skiff's own browser emulator and host tests do (web/emu/felucca_web.c, tests/hostsim.c,
editor_test.c, backup_test.c) and replaces only the hardware: keys/LEDs/LCD, ADC (MASTER; battery full), NOR flash = a 1 MiB RAM image, USB = always configured (SysEx and MIDI out through usb.c's rings),
one core (MENU > CPU 2 CORES has no second core here), no 320 MHz switch, no USB audio, no TRS MIDI, no serial console, no updater (ota.c answers the identity handshake only).
Compiled with WASI SDK clang (include shim tools/wasm_shim/sys/wait.h).

